{"type":"message","id":"103a8d6d","parentId":"e38d51d9","timestamp":"2026-05-18T09:42:49.448Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_gJbQJMhYQzE5oHppJzEV0pbo","toolName":"memory_search","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"6195b5d4daa96595230b975cc299ec27a2e7ff9df2bc4797cd62eb969ec02b17\",\n      \"path\": \"memory/2026-05-18-chart-fix.md\",\n      \"startLine\": 34,\n      \"endLine\": 85,\n      \"score\": 1,\n      \"textScore\": 0.565458822618258,\n      \"snippet\": \"The Google Doc did not include charts because:\\n\\n- the chart file was **invalid**\\n- the pipeline **removed it**\\n- the article placeholders were **never converted into actual chart image embeds**\\n- the DOCX builder only embedded the **feature image**, not the chart\\n\\n### In short\\n\\nThis run failed for **both** reasons:\\n- **chart generation failed**\\n- **DOCX export logic does not currently inject charts into the placeholders**\\n\\n### Best fix\\n\\nI’d recommend changing the pipeline so that before `pandoc` runs, it:\\n\\n- checks whether `/tmp/chart.png` is valid\\n- replaces each `[CHART_PLACEHOLDER]` in a temporary export file with markdown like:\\n  - `![Price Chart](/tmp/chart.png)`\\n- if the chart is inval\\n\\nSource: memory/2026-05-18-chart-fix.md#L34-L85\",\n      \"source\": \"memory\",\n      \"citation\": \"memory/2026-05-18-chart-fix.md#L34-L85\",\n      \"corpus\": \"memory\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"973d7f3aab310a8e890a62338c101fd3dc921badaa0842e352c6973936d509b5\",\n      \"path\": \"memory/2026-05-18-chart-fix.md\",\n      \"startLine\": 86,\n      \"endLine\": 86,\n      \"score\": 1,\n      \"textScore\": 0.5233181917187623,\n      \"snippet\": \"\\\"body\\\": \\\"I checked the actual run, and the main reason is clear:\\\\n\\\\nWhy the chart was not included\\\\n\\\\n1. The chart generation step failed validation\\\\n  • The chart agent returned CHART_DONE: /tmp/chart.png\\\\n  • But validation immediately failed with: CHART_INVALID: not a PNG\\\\n  • After that, the pipeline deleted /tmp/chart.png and continued.\\\\n2. The article still contains raw chart placeholders\\\\n  • /tmp/crypto-article.md still has 2 occurrences of:\\\\n    • [CHART_PLACEHOLDER]\\\\n3. The DOCX export only added the feature image\\\\n  • The export step used:\\\\n    • ![Feature Image](/tmp/crypto-feature.jpg)\\\\n  • It did not replace [CHART_PLACEHOLDER] with an actual image reference for the chart.\\\\n4\\n\\nSource: memory/2026-05-18-chart-fix.md#L86\",\n      \"source\": \"memory\",\n      \"citation\": \"memory/2026-05-18-chart-fix.md#L86\",\n      \"corpus\": \"memory\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"1735cb0b6406180efdcff3fd170dab1524b3b14a9ea429ede0d63b5475a8b9df\",\n      \"path\": \"memory/2026-05-18-chart-fix.md\",\n      \"startLine\": 86,\n      \"endLine\": 87,\n      \"score\": 1,\n      \"textScore\": 0.5233181917187623,\n      \"snippet\": \"\\\"body\\\": \\\"I checked the actual run, and the main reason is clear:\\\\n\\\\nWhy the chart was not included\\\\n\\\\n1. The chart generation step failed validation\\\\n  • The chart agent returned CHART_DONE: /tmp/chart.png\\\\n  • But validation immediately failed with: CHART_INVALID: not a PNG\\\\n  • After that, the pipeline deleted /tmp/chart.png and continued.\\\\n2. The article still contains raw chart placeholders\\\\n  • /tmp/crypto-article.md still has 2 occurrences of:\\\\n    • [CHART_PLACEHOLDER]\\\\n3. The DOCX export only added the feature image\\\\n  • The export step used:\\\\n    • ![Feature Image](/tmp/crypto-feature.jpg)\\\\n  • It did not replace [CHART_PLACEHOLDER] with an actual image reference for the chart.\\\\n4\\n\\nSource: memory/2026-05-18-chart-fix.md#L86-L87\",\n      \"source\": \"memory\",\n      \"citation\": \"memory/2026-05-18-chart-fix.md#L86-L87\",\n      \"corpus\": \"memory\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c14a5e12b8ace2f56a0a842a6b26151867b25c0838a12025184cbce6ce9ce07b\",\n      \"pa