ut a market structure event, with leveraged longs getting squeezed as external risk headlines and broad selling pressure fed into each other. The repeated use of phrases like ‘flash crash,’ ‘sell-off,’ ‘macro storm,’ and ‘liquidations’ suggests the move was abrupt, crowded, and amplified by derivatives positioning. The more specific liquidation figures are especially important: $500 million liquidated in an hour in one report, $584 million across 24 hours in another, and $160 million across the network in one hour in a Bitget summary. That combination of short-window and 24-hour figures indicates sustained stress rather than a single isolated spike. The market narrative also links Bitcoin’s slide to macro headlines about Iran and U.S. policy, which likely intensified the risk-off response among traders. Even where the wording differs by source, the core event is the same: Bitcoin’s drop below $77,000 triggered a heavy liquidation wave and dragged the broader crypto market lower.\\\",\\n  \\\"CHART_COIN\\\": \\\"bitcoin\\\"\\n}\\nJSON\\nrm -f ~/.openclaw/agents/writer/sessions/sessions.json\\nopenclaw agent --agent writer --message \\\"First, read the COINOGRAPHY_TEMPLATE.md file in your workspace to learn your strict formatting rules. Then, write a 1100-1200 word crypto news article using these facts: $(cat /tmp/research.json). You MUST finish the article completely, ending with the Sources and Word Count block.\\\" --deliver > /tmp/crypto-article.md\\nsed -i '/<thinking>/,/<\\\\/thinking>/d' /tmp/crypto-article.md\\nif ! grep -qi \\\"Word Count:\\\" /tmp/crypto-article.md; then\\n  echo \\\"Article incomplete. Forcing recovery run...\\\"\\n  rm -f ~/.openclaw/agents/writer/sessions/sessions.json\\n  openclaw agent --agent writer --message \\\"Your previous attempt was cut off. Re-read COINOGRAPHY_TEMPLATE.md and write a tighter article using $(cat /tmp/research.json). You MUST reach the final Word Count block.\\\" --deliver > /tmp/crypto-article.md\\n  sed -i '/<thinking>/,/<\\\\/thinking>/d' /tmp/crypto-article.md\\nfi\\nword_count=$(wc -w < /tmp/crypto-article.md)\\nif [ \\\"$word_count\\\" -gt 1500 ]; then\\n  echo \\\"Article is too long ($word_count words). Forcing summarization pass...\\\"\\n  rm -f ~/.openclaw/agents/writer/sessions/sessions.json\\n  openclaw agent --agent writer --message \\\"Your previous draft was mathematically too long ($word_count words). Re-read COINOGRAPHY_TEMPLATE.md. Condense and summarize this exact text to be roughly 1100 words. Keep the same structure but shorten every paragraph aggressively.\\\" --deliver > /tmp/crypto-article-summarized.md\\n  sed -i '/<thinking>/,/<\\\\/thinking>/d' /tmp/crypto-article-summarized.md\\n  mv /tmp/crypto-article-summarized.md /tmp/crypto-article.md\\nfi\\nwc -w /tmp/crypto-article.md\\nhead -n 40 /tmp/crypto-article.md\\n```\\n\\nUse:\\n`/approve 7b6ec432 allow-once`\"}],\"api\":\"openai-completions\",\"provider\":\"local-bifrost\",\"model\":\"gpt-5.4\",\"usage\":{\"input\":12909,\"output\":1844,\"cacheRead\":22912,\"cacheWrite\":0,\"totalTokens\":37665,\"cost\":{\"input\":0,\"output\":0,\"cacheRead\":0,\"cacheWrite\":0,\"total\":0}},\"stopReason\":\"stop\",\"timestamp\":1779082753618,\"responseId\":\"chatcmpl-Dgkz7koo2j7sRat2zaGVT5r3LBXg1\"}}\n\nProcess exited with code 0.[... 16112 more characters truncated]"}],"details":{"status":"completed","sessionId":"dawn-trail","exitCode":0,"aggregated":"**: 10f45462-5d8c-41cc-8988-8fd90369afce\\n- **Source**: telegram\\n\\n## Conversation Summary\\n\\nassistant: [[reply_to_current]] ✅ Article written, generating chart...\\nassistant: [[reply_to_current]] ✅ Chart generated, generating feature image...\\nass\\n...[truncated]...\\n```\\nEND_QUOTED_NOTES\\n...[additional startup memory truncated]...\\n\\nA new session was started via /new or /reset. Execute your Session Startup sequence now - read the required files before responding to the user. If BOOTSTRAP.md exists in the provided Project Context, read it and foll